            <div xml:id="d286">

                <pb facs="0383" n="275" xml:id="pg275"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/530: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-04-01T18:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 1, 1927—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 1—10:35
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>315. Following from American consul at Hankow: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“March 31, 4 p.m. <hi rendition="#italic">Shasi</hi> sailed this morning
                            for Shanghai with 12 Americans including 4 women. <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Tungwo</hi> will sail tomorrow morning with
                            approximately 40 Americans. Foreign banks and newspapers still closed
                            and business practically at a standstill with no immediate prospects of
                            improvements.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
